From d02cafafdaeaca95707a9af68c3106380277e7c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: root <root@gbt350-odcdh2-a12-1.png-odc.dcgpu>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:06:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] online quant: MXFP4 with macro block scaling (mxfp4_mbs) on a
 Triton GEMM

Adds the `mxfp4_mbs[<block>][_a|_w]` online quantization formats: MXFP4
(1x32 E8M0) plus an 8-bit mantissa factor per macro block of K, as in
arXiv:2603.08713. Activations take the static factor (MBS-S) in the
quantization kernel; weights search ATOM_MBS_WEIGHT_CANDIDATES factors at
load time (MBS-D, 16 by default). The GEMM rescales the accumulator by the
factor ratio entering each macro block, so it keeps one accumulator and
costs 2 FP32 multiplies per output per macro block (1 one-sided).

- atom/model_ops/mxfp4_mbs.py: quantization and GEMM Triton kernels on the
  production layouts (row-major A, 16x16-preshuffled B, shuffled E8M0),
  tile configs tuned on MI355X for Qwen3.5-9B shapes in
  mbs_gemm_configs.json.
- LinearBase: MBS branch in online_quantize_weight, custom op
  gemm_mxfp4_mbs in forward. Dense layers only; fused MoE falls back to
  plain MXFP4 with a warning.
- quant_spec: MBSSpec and LayerQuantConfig.mbs, parsed from the format
  string.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
