 `per_block_fp8` is DeepSeek-style block FP8: the weight uses a 128×128 block
 scale of shape `(N//128, K//128)` and the activation uses a 1×128 (along K)
 scale, consumed by the block-scale GEMM. `per_block_fp8` and `per_block128_fp8`
 are equivalent (128 is the default block size).
 
+### MXFP4 with macro block scaling
+
+`mxfp4_mbs` is MXFP4 with Macro Block Scaling
+([arXiv:2603.08713](https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.08713)). On top of the 1x32 E8M0
+block scales, every macro block of consecutive K values in a row carries an
+8-bit mantissa factor f = 1 + m/256. The block is multiplied by f before MXFP4
+quantization, which lines its largest value up with the FP4 grid, and the GEMM
+divides each macro block's partial sum by f_activation * f_weight in FP32. It
+runs on the MI355X MXFP4 MFMA; the E8M0 scales stay as in `mxfp4`.
+
+| Format string | Macro block | Factors on |
+|---|---|---|
+| `mxfp4_mbs` | 128 | activations and weights |
+| `mxfp4_mbs256`, `mxfp4_mbs512`, `mxfp4_mbs1024` | 256 / 512 / 1024 | activations and weights |
+| `mxfp4_mbs_a`, `mxfp4_mbs256_a` | 128 / 256 | activations only (weights are plain MXFP4) |
+| `mxfp4_mbs_w`, `mxfp4_mbs256_w` | 128 / 256 | weights only |
+
+- Activations take the static factor from their macro block's absolute maximum
+  (MBS-S). Weights are quantized once at load time and search
+  `ATOM_MBS_WEIGHT_CANDIDATES` factors (default 16) for the smallest squared
+  error (MBS-D).
+- Quantization and GEMM are Triton kernels (`atom/model_ops/mxfp4_mbs.py`, tile
+  configs tuned for MI355X in `atom/model_ops/mbs_gemm_configs.json`), not the
+  aiter asm GEMM that `mxfp4` uses. Every macro block costs the GEMM 2 FP32
+  multiplies per output (1 with one-sided factors), so larger macro blocks and
+  one-sided factors are faster.
+- Dense Linear layers only. The weight must be 2D with K divisible by
+  max(block, 256) and N by 16; exclude anything else, e.g. the Qwen3-Next /
+  Qwen3.5 GDN `*conv1d*`. Fused MoE experts are quantized as plain MXFP4 with a
+  warning. An activation that a fused norm+quant already produced is plain
+  MXFP4 and carries no factors.
+
+```bash
+python -m atom.entrypoints.openai_server \
+  --model Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B -tp 1 \
+  --online_quant_config '{
+    "global_quant_config": "mxfp4_mbs",
+    "exclude_layer": ["lm_head", "*visual*", "*conv1d*"]
+  }'
+```
+
